* Generate blocks for DR plasma rate coefficient computations: 

  In the cascade approach JenaAtomicCalculator.Basics.AverageSCA(), the following assumptions/simplifications are made: 
    + orbitals are generated independently for the first block in a Dirac-Fock-Slater potential; 
    + these orbitals are re-used for all other block, together with hydrogenic orbitals for the outer part; 
    + all blocks (multiplets) are generated from single-CSF levels and without any configuration mixing even in the SC; 
    + only the Coulomb interaction is considered for the electron capture. 
    + only E1 excitations are considered for the stabilization. 

